 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Of course. Gluten free means there are new details to think about. Does your roommate eat some gluten sometimes? If so, what would be the main meal of the week? Lots of people do switch up breakfast and lunch between gluten and gluten free. It' the dinner you want avoid. Pasta, bread, cakes, pastries, basically anything with wheat as an ingredient. Then you both need to stick gluten free dinners together, or you can each order in from the same place. Is there one you both like? It's worth trying again, usually there's gluten free fish, vegetables, and often rice or couscous.",
